# musl + true static-PIE. arch's musl-gcc.specs picks Scrt1.o (dynamic PIE
# start) and hardcodes -dynamic-linker, which yields a binary that links
# clean and segfaults. this swaps in rcrt1.o (self-relocating) and links
# static with no interpreter.
%rename cpp_options old_cpp_options

*cpp_options:
-nostdinc -isystem /usr/lib/musl/include -isystem include%s %(old_cpp_options)

# -fstack-protector-strong: musl's static libc provides __stack_chk_fail and
# canary setup, so SSP works in a no-ldso static-pie binary. -fstack-clash-
# protection emits stack probes (pure codegen, no libc dependency).
# NOT -D_FORTIFY_SOURCE: musl ships no _chk implementations, so it is a silent
# no-op -- fortify-headers would be a new dependency for a claim nothing backs.
*cc1:
%(cc1_cpu) -nostdinc -isystem /usr/lib/musl/include -isystem include%s -fstack-protector-strong -fstack-clash-protection

*link_libgcc:
-L/usr/lib/musl/lib -L .%s

*libgcc:
libgcc.a%s %:if-exists(libgcc_eh.a%s)

*startfile:
%{!r:/usr/lib/musl/lib/rcrt1.o /usr/lib/musl/lib/crti.o crtbeginS.o%s}

*endfile:
%{!r:crtendS.o%s /usr/lib/musl/lib/crtn.o}

# -r (partial link) cannot take -pie, and busybox partial-links every
# subdirectory, so the static-pie flags must apply to the final link only.
# -z noexecstack is kernel-enforced (non-exec stack) and gated by G16. relro/now
# emit PT_GNU_RELRO but nothing enforces it in a static-pie binary with no ldso
# -- kept as belt, deliberately NOT gated, so no check claims what it can't.
*link:
-nostdlib %{!r:%{!shared:-static -pie --no-dynamic-linker -z noexecstack -z relro -z now}} %{shared:-shared} %{rdynamic:-export-dynamic}
